  "oracle": "If n qualifies and n+1 is not prime, n+1 also qualifies, so the maximum is 1 or prime-1. Bytearray sieve to 2*10^6+1 and constructed (mirrored) palindromes give (pi,rub) at each candidate prime-1; suffix records with strictly decreasing pi/rub (descending n) are binary-searched with exact q*pi<=p*rub. LIMIT=2*10^6 is justified by test_no_qualifying_n_between_limit_and_ten_million (numpy sieve to 10^7: every candidate prime-1 in [2*10^6,10^7] has pi>42*rub) and test_rosser_tail_beyond_ten_million (pi(n)>=n/ln n for n>=17; rub(n) linear upper bound per digit-length d; n/ln n minus that bound is concave so endpoint checks at 10^(d-1),10^d with ln(10^k)<=k*2.302585094, exact integer arithmetic for d=8..1000; beyond that 10^(d-1)/(2.31d) dwarfs 42*11*10^(d/2)).",
